; recordarrive.eval - a monster placed on a BROWSED level arrives as placed,
; whatever the level's last record went through, and an erase of a record the
; level's held state speaks for can be undone (code-review C327). Judged by
; tools/EditorTest.py phase 32, on a scratch copy of dungeon-demo.
;
; eval_arena's last record is the swarm at 13,13. It is killed, the party goes
; down to crypt1 (eval_arena's state - the swarm dead - is held for it, under
; the swarm's record id), and from there the editor works on the browsed
; eval_arena. `editor records` prints each record on a square with its id and
; whether the held state names that id (held=1).
; 1. UNDO. The swarm's record erased and the erase undone: the record is back
;    with its id, and its held death with it - the erase used to drop the
;    diff, which the undo snapshot (the ACTIVE level's state only) could not
;    bring back, so the swarm stood up alive on the way back.
; 2. A NEW ID. The swarm's record erased again and a skeleton placed at 15,15:
;    a new record took max(id)+1, so it was handed the erased swarm's id, and
;    on the way back the held state for that id - dead, at 13,13 - was laid on
;    the skeleton: it arrived a corpse on the swarm's square.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 11
freeze on
tp 13 12
face s
effect bleed ahead 999 2
step 1
echo --- killed ---
monsters
goto crypt1
editor
levels view eval_arena
editor records 13 13
editor erase 13 13
undo
levels view eval_arena
echo --- undone ---
editor records 13 13
goto eval_arena
echo --- back ---
monsters
goto crypt1
editor
levels view eval_arena
editor erase 13 13
editor place monsters skeleton 15 15
echo --- placed ---
editor records 13 13
editor records 15 15
stashes
goto eval_arena
echo --- arrived ---
monsters
echo --- end ---
